  "id": "DrugBank_DB06650 - MONDO_2083",
  "verbalization": "Ofatumumab, a monoclonal antibody, is linked to Richter Syndrome through its role in Acute Lymphoblastic/lymphocytic Leukemia (ALL), as evidenced by multiple indirect pathways. The drug is indicated for ALL, and several related agents—Duvelisib, Uracil Mustard, and Obinutuzumab—are also indicated for Richter Syndrome. This suggests a potential pathway where Ofatumumab may influence the progression of ALL, which in turn could contribute to the development of Richter Syndrome. The evidence is supported by the shared indication for ALL and the subsequent indication for Richter Syndrome, indicating a possible mechanistic link between the drug and the syndrome. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of targeting the underlying disease process, such as the transformation of ALL into more aggressive forms, which may be a key mechanism in the relationship between Ofatumumab and Richter Syndrome.",
